Philipp Lucas wrote:
> Regarding "progress": I do not know whether nowadays anyone actually uses
> PatchHack and what those people would like to have integrated. Thus,
> PatchHack has not been updated for a few months.

The original Patchhacks had gameplay patches as well.  I really liked
the idea behind that.

SLASH'EM is somewhat cool, but I think it really suffers for being too
inclusive.  When I found out that Monks had "blitz"-style abilities
inspired by Final Fantasy III/VI, that the whip from Castlevania was in
the game, and the Deck of Many Things-like features of gypsies, I felt
like I had been hit with a Wand of Drain Interest.

On the other hand, while I can appreciate their role as gatekeepers,
and I tend to think better of the DevTeam's exclusionary policy towards
many patches than I did a couple of years ago, I still think the game
could use some new features.

And now there are some patches that are really, really cool, like Color
Alchemy, many aspects of Biodiversity and Lethe (except turncoat pets),
Heck2, and so on.  I think there's room for a Nethack variant that's
midway between Slash and vanilla, and for a while I thought that
Patchhack would become that.    I don't have problems these days with
compiling source, but getting all these patches reconciled with each
other is not always simple.

So, um, you can count this as a vote in favor of its continuation if
you like.

